{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/861107-looking-for-a-minimalist-system-ruleset-to-adapt-for-a-larp","id":861107,"title":"Looking for a minimalist system/ruleset to adapt for a LARP","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-07T09:45:24-07:00","id":861107,"title":"Looking for a minimalist system/ruleset to adapt for a LARP","content":"Hello all<br /> <br /> I have been running a Vampire LARP for half a year now, and I'm having a lot of fun doing that.<br /> <br /> However, I want to do a completely non-WoD one-shot (Imaging in Dogs in The Vinyard and Carnivale had a baby), and while freeforms are fun, I need some system to resolve disputes that need some non-talking solution. <br /> <br /> It need not be complex, in fact, the simpler, the better, but I need something that can at least represent the usual trifecta of physicality, social prowess, and mental acuity, and some influence/contacts/etc system.<br /> <br /> Any suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T16:44:14-07:00","id":861423,"title":"","content":"<b>End Of The Line</b> was the first test of a light LARP version of <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b>, and the rules for it are covered in <a href=\"http://rollespilsfabrikken.dk/cotlarp/dd/cotlarpdd.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">the preliminary information packet</a> for the next event <a href=\"http://www.cotlarp.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Convention Of Thorns</a>.<br /> <br /> Basically every relevant skill (like brawling) is rated 0-5 and players indicate character skill by holding up the appropriate number of fingers, while superhuman powers are covered by stock phrases like &quot;you really want to believe me&quot; with <i>really</i> being repeated to show the power level used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T02:47:34-07:00","id":861712,"title":"","content":"Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think that is two beers I owe you now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}